  "definition": "Additional Obligations of Mechanical Business Entities and Individual Fuel Gas Fitting Licensees, Plumbing Licensees",
  "effectiveDate": "2017-09-20",
  "historyNote": "#12385, eff 9-20-17; (formerly Saf-Mec 603.02) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 600)",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Mec 603.02",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Mec 603.02 Additional Obligations of Mechanical Business Entities and Individual Fuel Gas Fitting Licensees, Plumbing Licensees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 603.02 Additional Obligations of Mechanical Business Entities and Individual Fuel Gas Fitting Licensees, Plumbing Licensees. Licensees, certified oil heating and water treatment technicians, and mechanical business entities shall:\n\n(a) Obtain local permits and inspections as required;\n\n(b) Accurately inform their customers or potential customers in writing about any reasonably foreseeable hazards and potential code violations that may pose a risk of personal safety to them, to property owners, or to occupants;\n\n(c) Act in good faith to recognize, repair or remove from service any appliance or system that presents an imminent threat to the health or life safety of a property owner, resident, tenant, or visitor to the property, facility, or building which the licensee discovers in the performance of their duties; and\n\n(d) Honor any warranty of products or services whether implied or in writing as part of a sale of services, goods, or both, to consumers in a timely and proficient manner.\n\nSource. #12385, eff 9-20-17; (formerly Saf-Mec 603.02) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec600.html"
}
